# .env.example -- variable names only; every value is left empty
# Copy it to .env and fill it in (scripts/setup.sh copies it for you and never overwrites an existing .env).
# 🔒 .env is never committed. Share values through a password manager, never in chats, issues or PRs.

# ---- Run mode ----
# 1 = never call a paid API; everything runs on mock data and keyword rules. 1 is the default.
MOCK=1

# ---- External services ----
# The real runtime variables of the API Worker are in apps/api/.dev.vars.example
# (MOCK, LLM_API_KEY, LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_MODEL): wrangler dev reads apps/api/.dev.vars, not this file.
# The hosted LLM key was removed after the event, so the live API reads signs with keyword rules and
# the pre-computed readings that ship in apps/api/public/answers/demo.json.
# Purpose: which LLM to use | Module: apps/api | Without a value: keyword rules
LLM_MODEL=
# For every variable you add, document above it: purpose | module | where to get it | quota owner | behaviour without a value
# Example:
# Purpose: example API | Module: apps/xxx | Get it at: https://example.com/keys | Quota: @Zemmeng | Without a value: MOCK
# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=

# ---- Cloudflare ----
# Workers read .dev.vars in their module directory during local development (see apps/api/.dev.vars.example), not this file.
# Production secrets are set with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` and never stored in any file. See docs/architecture/deployment.md.
# Only the manual GitHub deploy workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) needs the two below, and they belong in the
# repository's GitHub Actions secrets, not here:
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Rule: whoever adds a variable adds a line here and documents it in the module README.
